---
import AnalyzerShell from '../components/AnalyzerShell';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Analyze Garage 61 stint exports locally in your browser without an account or backend."
    />
    <title>Garage 61 Stint Analyzer</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <!--
    THESIS: Turn local Garage 61 workbooks into one comparison sheet that refuses the dark neon dashboard.
    OWN-WORLD: Cool mineral paper, graphite ink, cobalt registration marks, and vermilion change signals form a calibration ledger.
    STORY: The visitor registers files, sees the driver gap, and traces each result to its supporting laps.
    FIRST VIEWPORT: A broad comparison sheet leads with the import state, readouts, and an empty evidence table; Export report sits in the top rail.
    FORM: Calibration Ledger, assigned direction candidate 3, seed key 7c2a91e4.
    FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, DESIGN.md, and every shipping raster carrying its provenance
    -->
    <AnalyzerShell client:load />
  </body>
</html>
